	still sizes the wall from EarthMagicMeshes.TerraKit.TR_Wall_Slab_01..12 (vfx_blocking/terra/WALL_TOMB_PORT_SPEC.md).

	AXES AND FRAMES. Every vector / CFrame here is in ROBLOX KIT axes (Blender (x, y, z) -> (-x, z, y)). The WALL FRAME's
	origin is the wall's base centre on the floor, +Y up, +Z = the front (the enemy side, where the showcase's hits land).
	Place it with   wallCF * Turn * <kit CFrame>   where wallCF is the live CFrame.lookAt(base, base + face) (its
	LookVector the front): Turn = CFrame.Angles(0, math.pi, 0) carries kit +Z onto the LookVector. The integrator may
	correct Turn after measuring the import (the setup script's pivot rows).
	PARTS. A piece is up to four MeshParts sharing ONE pivot (its Blender origin): Name, Name.._Brk (fracture faces, white),
	Name.._Lit (the lit 40% of the seams, white), Name.._Dead (the rest, white) -- any but the stone may be missing
	(ChargedRock.Clone). The setup script makes every PivotOffset a pure translation, so a part goes to pivot CFrame P
	with part.CFrame = P * part.PivotOffset:Inverse() (all parts of a piece take the same P). A scaled template piece:
	scale Size AND PivotOffset.Position by the same factors. The stone's colour is baked (white Color keeps it).

	FIELDS (spec section 2, plus the additions marked +):
	  Version, Turn, Size (the whole wall's box), Foot (+: the bottom course stands this far down in its slot; the
	    showcase roots it -0.5, so the top is at Size.Y + Foot), Rows (+: course height), Gap (+)
	  Slabs[i]  (i = 1..12, bottom course first, left to right as wallCF sees it: the live TR_Wall_Slab_%02d order)
	    Name, Home (slab frame in the wall frame: centre + tilt), Size, Course (1..3), Under (slab indices it rests on),
	    Coarse = { {Name, Rel (pivot in the slab frame), Vol (+), Phase (+), Interior (+, see Template)} },
	    Phase (+: the whole slab's pulse phase, radians: pulse = 1 + 0.15 sin(2 pi 0.8 t - Phase)),
	    TemplateScale (+: Size / Template.Size, per axis), Topple (+: {V, W} -- the showcase's launch when it comes
	    down whole, slab frame-free: wall-frame studs/s and rad/s, for the slab's own collapse)
	  Template  (the demo slab, Slabs[7], cut fine: struck slabs show it scaled)
	    Slab (+: which slab it was cut from), Size, Impact (the damage centre on its front face, slab frame), Hits (+: the
	    five showcase hit points, slab frame), Snap (+), Over/OverTau/OverW (+: the stage snap's overshoot,
	    1 + Over*exp(-a/OverTau)*sin(min(a/Snap,1)*pi/2 + OverW*a) past Snap), SagCreep/SagTime (+: stage 4's top creeping
	    on: Rel offset SagCreep * min(a/SagTime, 1)), KitAt (+: where the template sits in the FBX, for the setup check)
	    Pieces[p] = { Name, Rel (pivot in the template slab frame), Vol, Sag, Phase,
	      Stage[1..4] = CFrame, cumulative, in the template slab frame: the piece at stage st = slabCF * Stage[st] * Rel,
	      Release = {Hit, Kind ("chip"|"spall"|"chunk"), V, W} or nil (slab-frame velocity / spin, g = Collapse.G),
	      Burst (+) = {V, W} or nil: its launch at the break (WallDrop "Broken") if still on the slab,
	      Interior (+) = true for a cell with no outside: its stone part IS its break faces, baked INNER; no _Brk }
	    (A hit from BEHIND mirrors the tables front to back: spec 0.2.)
	  Raise, Sink, Hit (+: the struck-slab jolt), Collapse = {WaveSpeed, WaveDelay (+), G (+), Landings = { {Slab, Release,
	    V, W, Land, Pose (the slab frame at landing, wall frame), LandV, LandW, Wedged} } -- the showcase's pass 1 with
	    Slabs[7] struck; Release/Land are seconds after the break}, Ground = {Slot = { {Name, Rel, T, V, W} }, Rim = { {Name,
	    Rel, T, Lift, Roll, Sag, FarZ, Side} }, SlotHalf} (Rel: the plate's top centroid, wall frame; tops at Y = 0),
	  Dust (proposals, wall_build.md 3.7), Parts (+: MeshPart counts in the kit, to plan the 160-part budget).
	EVERY NUMBER HERE IS A PROPOSAL where it is look tuning (the showcase's T).
]]

